    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always seen math as a practical tool for problem-solving, not abstract theory. My vocational diploma taught me basic calculations, but I’ve used it in daily life—like budgeting for hiking trips or analyzing data from volunteering. I appreciate how it connects to real-world applications, even if I’m not a math expert.",
